 its intense sweetness. It is often mentioned in dietary recommendations for diabetes management, highlighting its potential benefits for individuals seeking healthier alternatives to sugar. As a natural sweetener, Taumatina (also known as Thaumatin, E957) serves as a suitable option for those looking to reduce sugar intake while still enjoying sweet flavors.", "ESTEVIA:Estevia is a natural sweetener that is particularly relevant in the context of dietary management for diabetes. It is derived from the leaves of the Stevia rebaudiana plant and is known by its food additive code E960. Estevia serves as a sugar substitute, providing a sweetening option that can help individuals manage their sugar intake while still enjoying sweet flavors.", "CICLAMATO:Cyclamate (E952) is a non-nutritive sweetener that is often used in combination with other sweeteners to enhance sweetness.", "NEOTAME:Neotame (E961) is an artificial sweetener that is chemically similar to aspartame but is much sweeter and used in low-calorie foods.", "ACESULFAMO DE POTASIO:", "CANADIAN DIABETES ASSOCIATION:The Canadian Diabetes Association is an organization that focuses on diabetes education, research, and advocacy in Canada.", "LOCKWOOD D:Lockwood D is an author who contributed to the literature on diabetes management and education.", "FREY ML:Frey ML is an author who contributed to the literature on diabetes management and education.", "GLANDISH NA:Glandish NA is an author who contributed to the literature on diabetes management and education.", "HISS RG:Hiss RG is an author who contributed to the literature on diabetes management and education.", "BERGENTAL RM:Bergenstal RM is an author who contributed to the management guidelines for diabetes care.", "BUSE JB:Buse JB is an author who contributed to the management guidelines for diabetes care.", "DIAMANT M:Diamant M is an author who contributed to the management guidelines for diabetes care.", "NAUCK M:Nauck M is an author who contributed to the ma